# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles are executed by Linux containers and CI, where a
# CRLF line ending is a syntax error (`set: -\r: invalid option`), not a cosmetic
# difference. Windows checkouts have core.autocrlf=true, so without this every
# .sh in docker/ and packaging/ arrives with CRLF and a local Docker build dies
# in its first RUN. CI never noticed: its runners check out on Linux.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
